{"ts":"2026-08-10T14:52:16.870Z","type":"quest-declared","sealed":{"doneWhen":{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/partition-callback-read-failure-typed-outcome.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["failed-partition-reads-surface-typed-outcomes","callback-reads-ride-routed-delivery-priority"]}},"frontierMetrics":[{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/partition-callback-read-failure-typed-outcome.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["failed-partition-reads-surface-typed-outcomes","callback-reads-ride-routed-delivery-priority"]}}],"authoringContractVersion":1,"statement":"A failed partition-callback read surfaces as a typed owner outcome, never as a clean empty result: PartitionCallbackDispatcher partitions its per-partition results instead of filtering them (failedPartitions carrying partitionId/error/errorCode/participantNodeId/retryAfterMs/backpressured from the existing buildPartitionExecutionFailureResult fields), returns a non-success outcome when every partition failed, and carries failedPartitions through executePartitionCallback into hostResult so artifacts record '1 partition, 1 failed' instead of totalPartitions 0; callback reads also pass executionOptions (tableName + resolveRoutedDeliveryPriority) so system-table callback reads ride the same critical delivery lane and table attribution as executeSelect; and the examples-catalog scenario's anti-affinity inversion (non-seed-first candidate order discarding the resolved replica host when it is the seed) is corrected so the resolved host is the first candidate, with the zero-partition response becoming a thrown failover trigger for free. Verified at HEAD 5da367c47 across four archived runs (ec-final-20260810T14*): the two failing runs show 7 and 3 in-window ACK timeouts delivering to nodes-p1 replicas on the stalled seed (event-loop gaps 1.1-1.9s, ELU 0.91-0.97) with zero timeouts in the two passing runs; the dispatcher's success-only filter (partition-callback-dispatcher.js:138-145) converts the total failure to success:true/batches:[] (hostResult totalPartitions 0), test-locked at partition-callback-dispatcher.test.js:122; nodes-p1 replicas never left the seed in any run (placement/lag/split sub-faces refuted by snapshots). ARCH-0139: missing rows must surface as typed owner outcomes; the sibling executeSelect path already propagates partition failure correctly. Fail-closed floor: partial success (some partitions failing) stays a typed partial outcome, never all-or-nothing data loss; the ReadIndex named wheel is explicitly out of scope (reads failed on transport, not staleness).","title":null,"class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."}],"verificationTemplates":["transport-delivery","harness-fidelity"],"frontierIds":["partition-callback-read-failure-typed-outcome-main"]}}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T15:16:36.799Z","type":"attempt","frontier":"partition-callback-read-failure-typed-outcome-main","rung":"observe","rungIndex":1,"prevRungIndex":0,"hypothesis":"PartitionCallbackDispatcher partitions per-partition read results instead of filtering to successes: failed reads become typed participant failure entries (buildParticipantFailureEntry, the same owner executeSelect uses), an all-reads-failed dispatch returns a non-success typed outcome (PARTITION_CALLBACK_ALL_READS_FAILED + DISTRIBUTED_PARTICIPANT_FAILURE + deferRetry/retryAfterMs from the first entry), and executePartitionCallback folds partial read failures into hostResult (totalPartitions/failedPartitions count every resolved partition; failedPartitionReads carries the typed entries) or synthesizes the failed aggregate without invoking the callback host when no batch exists. Callback reads now pass executionOptions {tableName, deliveryPriority: resolveRoutedDeliveryPriority(tableName)} so system-table callback reads ride the critical lane with failedTable attribution. examples-catalog buildCandidateNodeOrder anti-affinity inversion fixed: the resolved replica host is always the first candidate; the typed non-success outcome rejects the harness client promise (error envelope -> _resolvePendingQuery reject) so failover engages without consumer changes. Receipts 2/2; red-on-revert verified per-mechanism (dispatcher success===false assertion, integration hostResult counts, scenario candidate-order assertion); neighbors green (16 files, 1500+ assertions); eslint/literals/silent-catch/duplication/cycles/unused-exports clean; dispatch complexity kept <=12 via partitionReadResults extraction and executePartitionCallback reduced 35->29 via resolveCallbackRuntimeRegistry extraction.","changeRef":"diff:solve/changes/partition-callback-read-failure-typed-outcome/attempt-1.diff","metricBefore":null,"metricAfter":0,"metricDirection":"lower-is-better","invalidSample":false,"baselineAbsent":true,"done":tr